# Sources of the semantic-machinery study (hub 4.5). Locators that begin with 'txt' are line numbers in the study's pdftotext copy of a PDF.

n: 2.15
name: semantic-machinery-sources
kind: hub
is: The study report on choice, objects, identity and boundaries, the first-round critique, and 31 published sources its encoded claims cite: 6 PDFs and 25 web pages and repository files. The study read the web pages through a summarising fetch; 29 of the 31 were read again while encoding, as local text copies or raw page bytes.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/web-semantics-machines

n: 2.15.1
name: web-semantics-machines.md
kind: source
is: The first-round study report 'Semantic machinery one grammar must carry natively', 352 lines: control, object model and generics, identity and boundaries, each with prior art, a smallest sufficient set, a cost table and proposals R1 to R22.
path: coherence-seed/study/r1/web-semantics-machines.md
date: 2026-11-24
got: 2026-11-24
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/web-semantics-machines

n: 2.15.2
name: critic.md
kind: source
is: The completeness critique of the first study round, 471 lines: gaps G1 to G15, 47 spot-checks, contradictions C1 to C12 between reports, and what is ready and not ready to decide.
path: coherence-seed/study/r1/critic.md
date: 2026-11-24
got: 2026-11-24
at: 2026-11-24
by: r1/web-semantics-machines

